QEMU 11.1.1 linux-user: madvise(MADV_GUARD_INSTALL) answers 0.

paslang's runtime puts a guard page under every stack with
madvise(addr, 4096, MADV_GUARD_INSTALL) (102, Linux 6.13) and stops
when it fails; QEMU 11.1.1 answers EINVAL for advice it does not know.
Under QEMU the call succeeds and installs no guard, as the binary patch
scripts/patch-qemu-madv102.py did before P226. Only 102: any other
advice QEMU does not know still fails.

--- a/linux-user/mmap.c
+++ b/linux-user/mmap.c
@@ -1353,6 +1353,9 @@
     case -1:    /* BoringSSL uses -1 to check if the environment is broken */
         ret = -EINVAL;
         break;
+    case 102:   /* MADV_GUARD_INSTALL (Linux 6.13): not emulated, no guard */
+        ret = 0;
+        break;
     default:
         qemu_log_mask(LOG_UNIMP, "Unhandled madvise(%d) call.\n", advice);
         ret = -EINVAL; /* not yet known advise */
